# Testing

This file is the root testing entrypoint. Keep product README instructions
short; record detailed MVP and slice procedures here and in the linked
`.orchestration/` evidence files.

## Toolchain

| Purpose | Tool/version | Command |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lint | <tool and pinned/declared version> | `<lint command>` |
| Build | <tool and pinned/declared version> | `<build command>` |
| Test | <tool and pinned/declared version> | `<test command>` |

Run in this order and stop at the first failure:

```text
<lint command>
<build command>
<test command>
```

## Environment rules

- Use local or disposable resources by default.
- Do not mutate production.
- A shared, paid, or externally mutable non-production test environment needs
  the exact bound `APPROVE TEST ENVIRONMENT <environment-id>` command.
- Never commit credentials, raw logs, or production data. Record sanitized
  evidence and artifact digests instead.

